  "answer_text": "Found 3 gene records for cystic fibrosis: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [2], Fc gamma receptor IIa [4] and transforming growth factor beta 1 [5], linked to 1 disease: Cystic fibrosis [3]. \n\nAdditional data is in Publication pmid: 35853636 [1]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Cystic fibrosis [3]. \n\nGene-to-disease mapping\n\nGene NCBIGene:1080, name: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [2]. Gene NCBIGene:2212, name: Fc gamma receptor IIa [4]. Gene NCBIGene:7040, name: transforming growth factor beta 1 [5]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis [6]. Pubmed title: 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis [41]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children [43]. Pubmed title: Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis [45]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes [47]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Cystic fibrosis [7]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Cystic fibrosis\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Asthma [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Bronchiectasis [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Clubbing of fingers [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Dehydration [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Diarrhea [12]. Medgen clinical_features: Hemoptysis [13]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatomegaly [14]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatosplenomegaly [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypercalciuria [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Male infertility [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Cirrhosis of liver [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Biliary cirrhosis [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Nasal polyposis [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Pancreatitis [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Cor pulmonale [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Rectal prolapse [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Steatorrhea [24]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic sinusitis [25]. Medgen clinical_features: Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency [26]. Medgen clinical_features: Recurrent pneumonia [27]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic lung disease [28]. Medgen clinical_features: Ileus [29]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced forced vital capacity [30]. Medgen clinical_features: Elevated sweat chloride [31]. Medgen clinical_features: Recurrent bronchopulmonary infections [32]. Medgen clinical_features: Failure to thrive [33]. Medgen clinical_features: Meconium ileus [34]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced forced expiratory volume in one second [35]. Medgen clinical_features: Decreased forced expiratory flow 25-75% [36]. Medgen clinical_features: Hyperpolarized transepithelial nasal potential difference [37]. Medgen clinical_features: Salty tasting skin [38]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Cystic Fibrosis [39]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [40]. Clinical trial name: A Study of Topical Danazol for the Treatment of Pain Associated With Fibrocystic Breast Disease [42]. Clinical trial name: Efficacy and Safety of ONCOXIN in Patients With Breast Fibrocystic Disease [44]. Clinical trial name: A Clinical Study on the Efficacy and Safety of the Treatment of Hyperplasia of Mammary Glands With Xiaoru Sanjie Capsule [46]. Clinical trial name: Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [48]. "
