    "reply": "Several genes are associated with the condition, including Gene NCBIGene:1080 [1]. Another associated factor is Gene NCBIGene:2212 [3]. An additional related locus is Gene NCBIGene:7040 [4].\n\n## Clinical Manifestations\nThe primary condition is medgen title: Cystic fibrosis [6]. Clinical presentations often include medgen clinical_features: Bronchiectasis [15]. Patients may also experience medgen clinical_features: Asthma [11]. Further pulmonary complications can include medgen clinical_features: Hemoptysis [28].\n\n## Hepatic Complications\nSystemic disease features can involve medgen clinical_features: Hepatomegaly [29]. Some individuals also present with medgen clinical_features: Hepatosplenomegaly [30]. Hepatic involvement frequently occurs, while neurological sequelae are unusual [26: \"Cystic fibrosis liver disease (CFLD) affects a large proportion of cystic fibrosis (CF) patients; however encephalopathy is a rare complication\"].\n\n## Relevant Research Trials\nCurrent clinical studies include Clinical trial name: Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [24]. Another ongoing investigation is Clinical trial name: Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [8]. Published medical literature explores related aspects such as pubmed title: 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis. [10].",
