    "reply": "The genes associated with this condition include Gene NCBIGene:1080, name: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1]. Another factor is Gene NCBIGene:2212, name: Fc gamma receptor IIa [3]. Additionally, it involves Gene NCBIGene:7040, name: transforming growth factor beta 1 [4]. The primary condition is Disease name: Cystic fibrosis [2].\n\n## Clinical Manifestations\nThe core concept is medgen title: Cystic fibrosis [6]. Associated symptoms include medgen clinical_features: Asthma [11]. Respiratory issues present as medgen clinical_features: Bronchiectasis [15]. Patients may also show medgen clinical_features: Clubbing of fingers [19]. Systemic issues include medgen clinical_features: Dehydration [23]. Gastrointestinal symptoms manifest as medgen clinical_features: Diarrhea [27]. Other pulmonary signs include medgen clinical_features: Hemoptysis [28]. Liver enlargement is noted as medgen clinical_features: Hepatomegaly [29]. Combined organ enlargement presents as medgen clinical_features: Hepatosplenomegaly [30]. \n\n## Scientific Literature\nThe entity is recognized as Literature entity name: Cystic Fibrosis [7]. A relevant reference is Publication pmid: 32800451 [9]. Another citation is Publication pmid: 35240644 [13]. Further evidence is Publication pmid: 35592838 [17]. Additional data is in Publication pmid: 35853636 [21]. A recent paper is Publication pmid: 39129918 [25]. Titles include pubmed title: Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis. [5]. Diet is covered in pubmed title: 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis. [10]. Pediatric focus is in pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children. [14]. Treatments are discussed in pubmed title: Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis. [18]. Comorbidities appear in pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes. [22]. Liver disease is frequent in this population [26: \"Cystic fibrosis liver disease (CFLD) affects a large proportion of cystic fibrosis (CF) patients\"]. However, brain involvement is infrequent [26: \"encephalopathy is a rare complication\"].\n\n## Clinical Trials\nOne study is Clinical trial name: Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [8]. Another evaluation is Clinical trial name: A Study of Topical Danazol for the Treatment of Pain Associated With Fibrocystic Breast Disease [12]. A related investigation is Clinical trial name: Efficacy and Safety of ONCOXIN in Patients With Breast Fibrocystic Disease [16]. Other research includes Clinical trial name: A Clinical Study on the Efficacy and Safety of the Treatment of Hyperplasia of Mammary Glands With Xiaoru Sanjie Capsule [20]. Reproductive considerations are studied in Clinical trial name: Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [24].",
